    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to welcome someone, establish relationships and resolve a misunderstanding about who is involved.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U4-01-skill-K-HSK4-listen-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 4: listen",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Track the participants, whether an action was deliberate and whether it was reciprocal. A contrasting result can limit an earlier positive statement without cancelling every part of it.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "故意",
                "pinyin": "gùyì",
                "meaning": "deliberately; on purpose",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "4c1a6a59a329f8cf574ae545fba0aedc3cd1ee642f78d41b47eda6a777df8ef5"
              },
              {
                "text": "互相",
                "pinyin": "hùxiāng",
                "meaning": "each other; mutually",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "1d47e6e8dc0f9eb26dde5ba68e1e8e8591f68e7acdd02ea895e1e99ba7b0bc25"
              },
              {
                "text": "却",
                "pinyin": "què",
                "meaning": "but; yet",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "39dc374d30e93d430143e2aa976daeb3798b47b0847d930fc49655cba6d855c6"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Two partners discuss an earlier situation. The first two statements are A’s; the last is B’s.\nFamiliar meanings available: deliberately; on purpose; each other; mutually; but; yet."
          }
        ]
      },
